2026-11-06  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	* lws-crypto.c (lwsjs_crypto_pbkdf2, lwsjs_crypto_hkdf,
	lwsjs_crypto_scrypt, lwsjs_crypto_argon2id): New.  Key derivation for
	Bun.password and crypto.subtle deriveBits.  pbkdf2, hkdf and scrypt
	use EVP_KDF; argon2id is built in (BLAKE2b and the RFC 9106 fill) as
	EVP_KDF only has ARGON2 from OpenSSL 3.2.

	* lws-crypto.h, doc/native/crypto.md: Document them.

	* tests/unittests/test-crypto.js: Add RFC 6070, 5869 and 7914 vectors
	and argon2id hashes made by Bun and libargon2.

	* lws-crypto.c, lws-crypto.h: New.  Native crypto primitives for
	building crypto.subtle in JS, on OpenSSL 3: digest, hmac (SHA-1/256/
	384/512) and ECDSA over P-256/P-384/P-521 (ecGenerateKey, ecPublicKey,
	ecValidatePoint, ecSign giving r||s, ecVerify).

	* lws.c (lwsjs_init, js_init_module): Export them as `crypto`.

	* tests/unittests/test-crypto.js: New.

	* doc/native/crypto.md: New.

	* lib/serve.js (serve): New options maxRequestBodySize and
	idleTimeout (Bun.serve).  idleTimeout calls server.timeout(); the body
	limit is handed to the http protocol.

	* lib/lws/protocols.js (HttpProtocol): New maxBodySize hook.  A
	request with a Content-Length above it is answered 413 without running
	the handler; a chunked body that grows past it fails the body stream
	with a RangeError.

	* tests/unittests/test-serve-body-limit-idle.js: New.

	* doc/js/bun.md, doc/api-compatibility.md: Document both options.

	* CMakeLists.txt (LIBWEBSOCKETS_C_FLAGS): Drop -std=cNN from the flags
	passed to the libwebsockets build.  With it clang 16+ rejects the
	"void main" snippets of lws's CHECK_C_SOURCE_COMPILES probes, so every
	LWS_HAVE_* was false: no pthread.h (lws_mutex_t unknown) and no
	sys/prctl.h (prctl undeclared) in the Termux builds.

	* libwebsockets: Moved to upstream main (6b0f392c8).  The submodule was
	pinned to a commit that only one checkout had, and its tree held the
	patches as uncommitted edits, so it could not be advanced.
	* patches/0004-termux-resolvconf.patch: Regenerated against the moved
	CMakeLists.txt context.
	* patches/0002-libwebsockets-sa46-pending-udp.patch,
	patches/0003-acme-sni-cert-q-keygen.patch,
	patches/0006-openssl-server-q-keygen-guards.patch,
	patches/0007-service-shutdown-no-parked-rx.patch: Removed.  Upstream
	now sends on a connected udp socket without a destination (0002), has
	the EVP_PKEY_Q_keygen guards (0003, 0006) and parks rx in LRS_SHUTDOWN
	(0007).

2026-11-05  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	* lws-protocol.c (lwsjs_callback_protocol): RECEIVE_CLIENT_HTTP with no
	JS handler drains the parked response body with lws_http_client_read().
	lws waits for that call before it reads again; a client protocol that
	only had onEstablishedClientHttp left the event pending, and lws was
	serviced over and over at full cpu for as long as the connection lived.
	* tests/unittests/test-client-http-no-drain.js: New.
	* tests/test-keepalive.js: Import setTimeout and clearTimeout from os
	(the suite did not run under the bare qjs).
	* BUGS: Note the cause of the busy loop in deferred-close-hangs-on-
	established-client-http, and the failed attempt to reproduce
	h1-late-queued-pipeline-never-promoted in plain libwebsockets.

	* lib/tcpsocketstream.js, lib/websocketstream.js, lib/udpsocketstream.js,
	lib/tcpsocket.js, lib/websocket.js, lib/udpsocket.js (ContextRefCounter
	destroy callback): Forget the shared context before destroying it.
	destroy() runs lws callbacks and, with them, the pending promise jobs; a
	constructor that ran among them found the dying context still set, made
	its connection on it, and lost the wsi when the destroy completed (a
	TCPSocketStream created right after the close of the previous one never
	opened, no event of any kind).  The adapter or socket table is only
	dropped if no new context was made meanwhile.
	* tests/unittests/test-tcpsocket.js: The TCPSocketStream test no longer
	awaits closed before the next test, which is the case that failed.
	* BUGS: Remove tcpsocketstream-connect-right-after-close-dropped.

	* patches/0008-h1-client-restart-queued-on-no-keepalive.patch,
	patches/0009-ws-rx-drain-after-bulk-keeps-callback.patch: Message
	rewritten for upstream: symptom, cause, fix, reproducer with
	before/after output (the diffs are unchanged).
	* patches/repro/h1-pipeline-no-keepalive.c,
	patches/repro/ws-deflate-large-message.c: New.  Standalone C
	reproducers against plain libwebsockets (no qjs-lws) for the two
	patches; each exits 1 without the patch and 0 with it.

	* patches/0009-ws-rx-drain-after-bulk-keeps-callback.patch: New.
	libwebsockets (lib/sansio/ws/ops-ws.c, lws_ws_rx_sm): the first drain of
	the permessage-deflate inflater after the bulk payload path had its
	output dropped, because NO_CB was cleared only while the wsi was on the
	draining list, which the entry drain had just left.  One lump of 1024
	bytes in five of every large deflated message was lost (a 70000 byte
	message arrived as 57712).
	* tests/unittests/test-ws-deflate-large-message.js: New.

	* lws-protocol.c (lwsjs_callback_protocol): HTTP_FILE_COMPLETION with
	no JS handler goes to lws_callback_http_dummy().  That is what completes
	the transaction of a served file: it resets the per-response state of
	the wsi.  Without it the next response on the kept-alive connection had
	its headers counted as body, "no room for file content", and the file
	was never sent (header, then close): fetch() of two files from an
	LWSMPRO_FILE mount failed on the second.
	* lib/lws/protocols.js (HttpClientProtocol#onEstablishedClientHttp):
	Ignore the established report that lws makes for a stream queued on an
	h2 connection before any response (status 0), and a repeat of it; the
	Response built for the first locked the body stream for the second
	("stream already locked").
	* tests/unittests/test-file-mount-keepalive.js: New.

	* lib/serve.js (serve): The ws protocol is now protocols[0] and forwards
	onHttpConfirmUpgrade to the http upgrade hook.  A client that sends no
	Sec-WebSocket-Protocol (Bun, browsers, ws, python websockets) is bound
	to the vhost's default protocol, so it got the 101 reply and then never
	reached open/message.  perMessageDeflate is passed on to the context
	and vhost; maxPayloadLength and publishToSelf go to WebSocket.protocol.
	* lib/websocket.js (WebSocket.protocol): New options publishToSelf (the
	sender gets its own ws.publish()) and maxPayloadLength (close with 1009
	above it), the Bun websocket options.
	* lib/lws/util.js (makeFireEvent): Return nothing.  The result of
	dispatchEvent() was returned from lws callbacks, and a non-zero return
	closes the connection: a TCPSocket client was closed after its first
	message (and the same for UDPSocket and WebSocket callbacks that return
	fire()).
	* tests/unittests/test-serve-ws-no-subprotocol.js,
	tests/unittests/test-serve-ws-options.js: New.

	* lws.c (lwsjs_functions): toArrayBuffer(view) without an offset
	returned an empty ArrayBuffer for a typed array; the length is now
	defaulted by get_offset_length() for any argument count.
	* tests/unittests/test-toarraybuffer.js: New.
	* tests/test-serve.js: A string body is sent with content-length like
	Bun, not chunked.

	* lws-protocol.c (pollfd_handler): Ask poll() for the real state of the
	fd and hand that to lws_service_fd().  quickjs runs one handler per
	ready fd and loop turn, the read handler first; a connecting socket
	whose peer closed or refused stays readable, so the write handler never
	ran, lws never finished the connect on POLLIN alone and the wsi hung
	until lws' 3 s timeout (the busy loop that made test-tcpsocket time
	out).
	* iohandler.c (iohandler_set): Clear an fd handler only when this
	context registered it.  The os handler table is keyed by fd number for
	the whole process, so a destroyed context closing its wsi late wiped
	the handlers of a socket of another context that had reused the number.
	* lws-context.c (lwsjs_context_method): destroy() clears the remaining
	fd handlers of the context; lws sends no DEL_POLL_FD for a wsi it has
	not closed yet.
	* tests/unittests/test-tcpsocket.js: Await closed at the end of the
	TCPSocketStream test (see BUGS tcpsocketstream-connect-right-after-
	close-dropped).
	* tests/unittests/test-response.js: Response.json() has no space before
	charset, like Bun.

	* ChangeLog: New, GNU style.
	* CLAUDE.md: New section ChangeLog (format, examples/ exempt); stage
	files by name.

	* lib/tcpsocket.js (TCPSocket.listen): The message callback no longer
	returns the result of dispatchEvent().  lws reads a non-zero return of
	a callback as "close the connection", so a server that wrote from its
	data handler lost the connection after the first message.

	* lib/serve.js (flush): Send a Date header and, for a body whose type
	is known, a default content-type, the way Bun does: text/plain;
	charset=utf-8 for a string, application/octet-stream for bytes, the
	type of a Blob, application/x-www-form-urlencoded for URLSearchParams.
	An in-memory string or byte body is now sent with content-length
	instead of streamed, so the connection can be kept alive.
	(Server#url, serve): Pass the iface 127.0.0.1 for the host name
	"localhost" (as Bun binds it); lws takes an interface name or an
	address, and with a host name listenPort stayed 0.
	* lib/lws/response.js (Response.json): Use "application/json;charset=utf-8".
	* lws-socket.c (lwsjs_headers_size): New.  Size of the header lines of
	a headers object.
	(lwsjs_socket_respond): Size the header buffer from the real headers
	(heap buffer when large) instead of a fixed 2 KB; a header that does
	not fit is an error and no longer dropped.  Chunked responses and the
	statuses 204, 304 and 1xx on h1 keep the connection alive (status line
	written without lws_add_http_common_headers, which answers
	"connection: close" for an unknown length).
	* tests/unittests/test-serve-bun-headers.js: New.
	* tests/unittests/test-large-response-headers.js: New.

	* lib/fetch.js (fetch): Retry once on a fresh connection when the
	request queued on the shared connection died with "server closed
	before responding", for bodies that can be sent again.
	(fetchOnce): New, the former body of fetch.
	(buildContext): Ask for 32 KB header buffers (maxHttpHeaderData).
	* tests/unittests/test-fetch-reuse.js: New.

	* lws-context.c (lwsjs_context_creation_info_fromobj): Read
	max_http_header_data.

	* lws-vhost.c (lwsjs_vhost_constructor): A callback mount that names a
	protocol which is not in the protocols list now throws a TypeError
	instead of creating a mount that never answers.
	* tests/unittests/test-vhost-bad-mount.js: New.

	* lws-socket.c (lwsjs_socket_write, lwsjs_socket_transaction_completed)
	(lwsjs_socket_long_poll_rxonly, lwsjs_socket_http_client_read)
	(lwsjs_socket_add_header, lwsjs_socket_client_http_multipart): Throw
	"socket is closed" when lwsjs_socket_destroy() has zeroed the wsi,
	instead of dereferencing a NULL pointer.

	* lws-protocol.c (lwsjs_callback_protocol): When wsi.close() is called
	from inside the ESTABLISHED or CLIENT_ESTABLISHED callback, run the JS
	closed handler ourselves, once: lws treats the connection as never
	opened and skips CLOSED, so onClosed() never ran.  The close code still
	goes out because the callback keeps returning -1.
	(pollfd_handler): Bound the forced-service loop to 64 rounds; the rest
	is picked up by the service tick, so a wsi that keeps asking for
	service can no longer starve JS timers.
	* lws-socket.h (LWSSocket): New bit closed_fired.
	* tests/unittests/test-ws.js: Passes now (no change to the file).

	* lib/websocket.js (WebSocket#send): The drain callback no longer
	returns the result of dispatchEvent().  lws closed the connection
	right after the first send().

	* lib/rpc/json-rpc-handler.js (handleSingleRequest): params is
	optional.  The message of a thrown error goes over the wire instead of
	"Server error", with the error's data or its name and message in data.

	* cmake/BuildLibwebsockets.cmake (build_libwebsockets): Pass the
	arguments after the legacy target name as step dependencies; the test
	"if(ARGN)" was never true inside a macro.
	* cmake/FindLibreSSL.cmake (find_libressl): Only query the libressl
	target when it exists; append LIBRARY_DIR to the install rpath, not
	the undefined LIBRARY_PATH.

	* tests/unittests/tinytest.js: TEST_ONLY=<substring> runs only the
	tests whose name contains it.  Print failures with console.log when
	console.error is missing (bare qjs).
	* tests/unittests/test-context-features.js: Pass the body before the
	headers to respond() (the other order sends an empty body) and resolve
	on the end of the HTTP transaction, not on the close of a kept-alive
	connection.
	* tests/unittests/test-udp-send-integration.js,
	tests/unittests/test-websocket-server-members.js,
	tests/unittests/test-websocket-static-methods.js: Import setTimeout,
	clearTimeout and exit instead of using the compat layer globals.
	* BUGS: Remove the fixed entries, file the new ones, note what could
	not be reproduced.

	* lib/logger.js, lib/lws/body.js, lib/rpc/common.js: A missing
	qjs-modules module (console, blob, bjson) is reported with a clear
